      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Georg Thieme Verlag KG Stuttgart, New York.",
        "AbstractText": "Translaminar approaches have been described for lumbar disc herniations which are displaced cranially or laterally into the neuroforamen. This technique provides the advantages of a minimally invasive approach with regard to postoperative instability or partial facet joint resection and avoids a medial arthrectomy. We describe this technique for the first time as an option for a caudally sequestrated disc herniation via a transaxillar sequesterotomy."
      },
